\keyeq{\mathcal E_{L}[\phi](t,s)}&\keyeq{{}=D_t\mathcal A-D_s\!\left(g\beta T_m+\frac{\phi_t}{\phi_s}\mathcal A\right).}\label{eq:M}
\end{align}

Why do \eqref{eq:P} and \eqref{eq:M} disagree? A parcel moving at speed $u=\phi_t$ records the material rate $b_t=(B_t+uB_x)(t,\phi(t,s))$, not the fixed-position bed rate $B_t$. Subtracting $(\phi_t/\phi_s)b_s$ strips out the bed-advection term $uB_x$, and that subtraction is what produces $-D_s((\phi_t/\phi_s)\mathcal A)$
